{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>He who discerns</b> — [it] teaches understanding to the house of the wicked, like: 'a man and his house' — and 'the house' is a hint to children. Another interpretation: 'He who discerns' stands, and the meaning is: he learns understanding because of the house of the wicked — that they do evil and pervert the way of uprightness — [so] that HaShem will pervert them and destroy them. And this is the correct one."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:58.218242373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}